// Change: new rule
// Title: Potential Binary Proxy Execution Via DbgSrv.EXE
// Sigma ID: f4c96109-01bd-401a-b7f3-981b38cc9ce4
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: RealFiras
// Date: 2026-11-19 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: defense_evasion, execution, T1127, T1218
// Description: Detects execution of Microsoft User-Mode Debugger Process Server (dbgsrv.exe) with parameters to
//   launch child processes or establish reverse debugging connections.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate debugging activities by developers or system administrators.
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/OtherMSBinaries/Dbgsrv/
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-hardware/drivers/debugger/dbgsrv-command-line-options
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/9a4da76d34494d300cb027517551755dc96cdade/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_lolbin_dbgsrv.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\dbgsrv.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "dbgsrv.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains " -c " or ProcessCommandLine contains " -c\"" or ProcessCommandLine contains "clicon=")
